230
00:18:13,973 --> 00:18:16,900
Let's land this. You
should now be able to say:

231
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:21,126
A reset moves the current
branch and writes ORIG_HEAD.

232
00:18:21,166 --> 00:18:26,360
--mixed also rewrites the index, and
--hard also rewrites tracked files.

233
00:18:26,700 --> 00:18:32,571
Commits left behind are in the reflog, staged
content survives as unnamed blobs that

234
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:38,482
git fsck --lost-found lists, and edits that
were never staged have no object and are

235
00:18:38,522 --> 00:18:38,834
gone.

236
00:18:39,174 --> 00:18:44,710
Before a hard reset I preview with git log,
git status -s and git diff HEAD, and I

237
00:18:44,750 --> 00:18:50,219
stash and branch if anything should survive.
To drop commits I type --keep, which

238
00:18:50,259 --> 00:18:55,863
carries my changes across or refuses. git
commit --amend is a soft reset plus a new

239
00:18:55,903 --> 00:18:58,515
commit, and it doesn't write ORIG_HEAD.

